How to review	A1	pplr and Apple Contacts: sync plan, @GENERATED@
How to review	A3	Review the Merged sheet. Change only the four shaded columns; leave the rest as they are.
How to review	A4	  Decision: Add (a new iCloud card), Update (bring the card up to date from pplr), Link only (the pplr URL and group, no field changes), No change, or Skip (leave this person out of Contacts).
How to review	A5	  Card: the card to update or link, as a ref from the Contacts sheet (C0123). Change it if the plan picked the wrong card; clear it for Add.
How to review	A6	  Dupes: other cards that are the same person, comma-separated refs. They are listed for merging, never deleted without asking.
How to review	A7	  Notes: anything else, eg keep the card's name.
How to review	A9	Rows run least certain first: Low, then Medium, then High. Low and Medium rows are shaded in the Confidence column.
How to review	A10	Update never removes anything from a card. pplr wins on name, company and role; its emails, phones and LinkedIn are added beside the card's own. Addresses, birthdays, notes and photos on existing cards are left alone.
How to review	A11	Add makes an iCloud card from pplr with its photo, and every card touched gets the pplr URL and the PPLR group.
How to review	A12	Nothing is written until the reviewed workbook is applied, after a .vcf backup of every card.
How to review	A14	Proposals:
How to review	A15	     1  Low / Add
How to review	A16	     1  Low / Update
How to review	A17	     2  Medium / Update
How to review	A18	     2  High / Add
How to review	A19	     3  High / Update
